<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    GH-783: a label must be followed by a statement before C23.

    last_case (clang -O0) is a switch whose last arm, case 7, is empty:
    its table entry is a jump-only block to the code after the switch.  The
    printer used to end the switch with the bare label `case 7:`; it now
    gets `break;`.

    skip_blanks (gcc -O2) enters its loop through a goto whose target is
    the end of the loop body, so the body used to end with the bare label
    `label_10ad:` before the `} while` brace.  The label now gets the null
    statement `;`.  Both shapes are errors ("label at end of compound
    statement") in C99/C11/C17.

    Source: last_case(unsigned selector, unsigned *out) { unsigned v = 1;
    switch (selector) { case 1: v = 7; break; case 3: v = 9; break;
    case 4: v = 13; break; case 6: v = 5; break; case 7: break;
    default: v = 21; break; } *out = v; }
    skip_blanks(char **cpp) { char *cp; for (cp = *cpp; *cp == ' ' ||
    *cp == '\t'; cp++) ; *cpp = cp; }
    The jump table sits at 0x10b8, after the code.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x1000"></bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1000" name="last_case"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1090" name="skip_blanks"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>parse line extern void last_case(uint4 selector, uint4 *out);</com>
  <com>parse line extern void skip_blanks(char **cpp);</com>
  <com>load function last_case</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function skip_blanks</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="Label statement x64 #1: the empty last case gets break" min="1" max="1">case 7:$
break;$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="Label statement x64 #2: the loop-end goto label gets a null statement" min="1" max="1">^label_10ad:$
^\s*;$
^\s*\} while</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="Label statement x64 #3: no label directly before a blank line or a closing brace" min="0" max="0">:$
^\s*\}?\s*$</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
